A||N||8||Haze_Performance||Cat. question..||||5||
Z||000000||Haze_Performance||11-17-2000||11:49 PM||||Im just wondering if anyone here has a mostly stock 2.8L with stock exhaust & NO cat. ??<P>If so did you feel a performance gain without the cat.?<P>Just wondering  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlogo1_1.gif">   <BR><B>"AHHHHH!!! All Fiero's don't start on fire you BONEHEAD!!"</B>||||reg||5
Z||000001||rockcrawl||11-18-2000||07:29 AM||||I'll be cutting mine out this afternoon because I suspect it is blocked. From my past experience (mostly with V8 trucks) removing the cat makes a noticeable difference every time. It also makes it a bit louder. <P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||7
Z||000002||Predator||11-18-2000||08:07 AM||||You guys don't have to pass emmisions in PA?<BR>In pretty most the whole state of Georgia you can't get a tag without passing an emmissions test. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfixit58||11-18-2000||08:45 AM||||I had to remove mine last weekend. I just installed a by-pass pipe. The car is definitely louder. I think it gained "bottom end" but it could be that I just got used to the feeling of a partially clogged/clogged cat.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000004||BBBAD GT||11-18-2000||09:24 AM||||IMO, I think the stock muffler with no cat sounds the best!  It just burbles all day long.  I did feel the upper RPM range was a bit more easier on the motor.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/BBBAD_GT_SIG.gif">    <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||robertjay||11-18-2000||09:44 AM||||I did feel some improved throttle response, but it could have been because it was going bad.  After about a year, I installed Rodney Dickman's Cat and it didn't make a noticeable decrease in HP.||||reg||1
Z||000006||kornholio||11-18-2000||09:49 AM||||When I bought my car, it had no cat and it was loud.  The only reason I put one back on is to try to quiet it down.  I didn't notice any loss of power and it didn't make it quieter at all.  It still rumbles.||||reg||1
Z||000007||rockcrawl||11-18-2000||07:23 PM||||I definately noticed an increase in performance without the cat, but the old one was shot and rattling around. I just busted up the catalyst and dumped it out, left the cat there so it looks like it's legal. It has a funny hollow sound now, but just a tad bit louder than before.<P> Actually there is no emissions testing in PA right now until they come up with a new testing system. When it finally hits, it's gonna hit us hard. In the part of PA where I live, we have never had emissions testing.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Master_Sushi||11-18-2000||10:02 PM||||What about with an iron duke?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Or should I not waste my time?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
